  "literature_notes": "All four ledger lines describe tags on intracellular termini of ADCY8. L1, L2, and L3 all report the same YFP-AC8 construct generated by cloning AC8 cDNA into pEYFP-C1, which places EYFP at the N-terminus of the insert protein. The ADCY8 N-terminus (residue 1) is firmly intracellular per the topology landmarks (INTRACELLULAR: 1\u2013181); there is no signal peptide, and the protein has a cytoplasmic N-terminus (type IIIb multi-TM topology). L4 reports a C-terminal 3C-YFP-TwinStrep fusion on full-length bovine AC8; the C-terminus of ADCY8 (residue 1251) is likewise intracellular (INTRACELLULAR: 915\u20131251). None of the ledger lines report a tag insertion in any of the six short extracellular loops (ECL1 203\u2013211, ECL2 266, ECL3 311\u2013320, ECL4 734\u2013740, ECL5 807\u2013832, ECL6 874\u2013898). Because no ledger line grounds an extracellular surface insertion, zero sites are proposed.",
